Z||000000||whamel||09-18-2000||09:21 AM||||Well, got home late this weekend and it kind of ruined my plans to do some of the major stuff I was thinking of doing to my GT this weekend ... so, with a little spare time and a lot of boredom, I did the '89 Grand Am brake conversion.  Pretty nice little upgrade in my opinion.  I'll document the whole thing on my website (as usual), but briefly here's what my thoughts are: (I only did the rears, machine shop wasn't open to do the fronts)<BR>1) Rear upgrade alone was better, but still sub-par for todays standards<BR>2) Do the 1994 full size blazer upgrade!  Now - go do it.  What are you waiting for?  It rocks.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I'm most impressed with this.<BR>3) This upgrade is just plain simple.<BR>4) I will be putting this on EVERY Fiero I get right off.<BR>5) I didn't really need that e-brake anyway.<P>     Oh, on another note - I saw a sweet (looked to be an '85) Fiero on 69 South north of Ft. Wayne last night.  Very nice!  Had to get up to about 95-100 to catch her though.<BR>Have fun,<BR>Wade||||reg||14
